  "text": "In August 2016 we converged on Iran. Seventeen of us said \"that the obama administration,\" peaking August 3. Sixteen of us said \"state sponsor of\" the same day. Then the figure: twelve of us said \"payment to iran,\" eleven said \"400 million cash,\" ten said \"400 million cash payment,\" peaking August 18. Ten of us reached for \"the state department,\" ten for \"of 400 million,\" ten for \"cash to iran.\" The phrase \"that the obama administration\" had first appeared among us on 2013-01-25, from Tim Walberg; \"400 million cash payment\" only on 2016-08-03. The sum stayed fixed across our mouths: 400 million, cash, to Iran, the same three components in the same order, the count of us saying each rising toward the middle of the month. We reported one transaction, and we reported it together.",
